PR title: Small fixes

Source: https://github.com/StanfordVLSI/dragonphy2/pull/126

PR description:
This PR addresses three open issues by implementing the following features:

1. SRAM dump trigger via register - option to trigger SRAM dump without an external pin
2. CDR update clamping - mode to limit Phase Interpolator (PI) code updates to +/-1
3. PI local encoder fix - resolves X-optimism in the int_Qperi component

Implementation details:
The contributor introduced a new 32-bit `misc_ctrl_bits` register to accommodate these features, with only 5 of 32 bits currently utilized. For SRAM dumping, setting bit [2] enables the feature while bit [3] toggles the internal dump_start signal. CDR clamping is enabled via bit [3], with adjustable clamp amounts through a `cdr_clamp_amt` register defaulting to +/-1.

The X-optimism fix was formally verified using JasperGold to ensure logical equivalence with the previous implementation. Additionally, a bug fix improved error reporting in make.py for JusTAG and genesis build failures.

